{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And blasted.</b> הלייא\"ש בְּלַעַ\"ז — scorched, withered; a term of mashkof, the [lintel] that is constantly struck by the door knocking against it." "<b>East wind.</b> An east wind — what they call בי\"סא בְּלַעַ\"ז."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {0 "the la'az הלייא\"ש is Old French haleis/hales, 'scorched, parched'; Rashi explains via מַשְׁקוֹף (lintel), which is habitually battered by the door — i.e., beaten down, withered.", 1 "the la'az בי\"סא is Old French bise, a cold north/east wind."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:54.190493555Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}